+The current receipt is stored at `~/.local/share/hapi-deploy/current.json`. Linux keeps exactly one production tree at `/mnt/cache/build-cache/hapi-production/current`: a deployment builds into `.staging-<release-id>`, renames the existing tree to `.previous`, moves staging into `current`, and deletes `.previous` after the health check passes. If activation fails, the previous tree is restored instead. Windows always runs `D:\hapi\bin\hapi.exe`: deployment stages the executable and desktop compatibility scripts together, preserves an explicit rollback set, stops `HAPI-background`, replaces the executable, migrates the stable desktop environment, waits for the new Runner and native bridge, and then refreshes a connected Codex desktop. A failure restores the previous binary, `windows-host.json`, desktop scripts and stable user settings. Windows stores its receipt and rollback data under `D:\hapi\state`.
 
