+The Windows Hub connectivity check runs before and after activation. Windows activation changes the HAPI Runner/native executable selection in `windows-host.json` and installs the shared-engine desktop launch configuration; Codex authentication, native history and dynamic browser authorization context remain owned by the existing user and desktop instance. The existing `HAPI-background` task performs the controlled runtime restart. Configuration, backend readiness, desktop refresh and real Edge/computer-control operations are reported as separate acceptance stages.
