+
+## Shared-engine desktop authorization context, 2026-10-28
+
+The official Codex desktop and the HAPI background engine have independent lifetimes. The engine runs in Session 0, while the desktop creates its browser authorization host and computer-control service in the logged-in user's session. HAPI therefore configures both `CODEX_APP_SERVER_WS_URL` and `CODEX_APP_SERVER_USE_LOCAL_DAEMON=1` in the user environment, and `launch-app.ps1` injects the same values into every HAPI-launched desktop process. The second setting makes the supported desktop initialization path send the current conversation's tool configuration to the shared engine. The stable desktop endpoint terminates at the Rust supervisor's secure relay; the relay forwards the desktop's live per-thread configuration and does not persist the executor ID, authorization pipe, verifying identity, or CUA native pipe directory.
+
+Browser authorization IDs, browser access pipe paths, verifying identities and `SKY_CUA_NATIVE_PIPE_DIRECTORY` are instance-scoped. HAPI removes stale user-level copies of those fields during migration and does not save their values in logs or deployment receipts. The desktop application remains responsible for creating and refreshing them. Keep its `require-browser-access.mjs` authorization and URL checks intact.
+
+A Windows release uploads the desktop scripts and tests with the executable. `deploy-release.ps1` backs up the previous executable, host configuration, desktop scripts and the stable endpoint, local-daemon flag and managed CLI path under `D:\hapi\state\rollback\<release>`. It installs the migration first, waits for the Session 0 Runner and native bridge, and only then requests a desktop refresh. If Codex was running before deployment, the release must observe a new `desktop-launch.json` for the current compatibility revision before activation succeeds. If no user desktop is connected, the migration remains ready for the next interactive logon and the receipt records that launch confirmation is pending.
+
+Rollback is explicit and keeps its evidence after a successful deployment:
+
+```powershell
+pwsh.exe -NoLogo -NoProfile -NonInteractive -File D:\hapi\scripts\deploy-release.ps1 -ReleaseLabel <release> -Rollback
+```
+
+Rollback restores the stable environment values and files, then restarts the backend. It requests the official launcher to refresh a desktop that is already running, because existing processes retain their previous environment. With no interactive user, desktop initialization waits for the next logon.
+
+`tests\desktop-compatibility.ps1` distinguishes configuration, task registration, current desktop launch and functional acceptance. It records only versions and whether required fields are present; it does not record authorization values, browser history or page text. `tests\app-cycle.ps1` runs three Start-menu-style desktop restarts and verifies that the Session 0 app-server PID remains unchanged and no interactive app-server is created. `tests\desktop-lifecycle.ps1` arms and verifies a real logoff/login or reboot transition. Arm it from the interactive desktop, perform the selected transition, and read `D:\hapi\state\desktop-lifecycle-acceptance.json` after the next logon.
+
+Edge and computer-control acceptance is a separate functional stage. The minimum run discovers Edge, creates a page on a fixed non-sensitive test site, reads a marker and follows a link; it then discovers a window, restores it if minimized, captures a new screenshot and performs a control click. A minimized-window or missing-coordinate result requires restoring the window and reacquiring state. Never reuse coordinates from a screenshot captured before that state change. Process liveness, a listening pipe and a tool name do not satisfy this stage.
+
+The compatibility behavior was verified against OpenAI.Codex package `26.1023.6123.0`, bundled plugin `26.1023.50603`, CUA runtime archive `0.0.35/20261022235854-0e24579b4572`, `@oai/cua` `0.2.6`, `@oai/cua-repl` `0.1.2` and `@oai/browser-desktop` `0.1.1`. The migration resolves the installed package directory each time and records the observed versions. A desktop update must rerun configuration and functional acceptance because `CODEX_APP_SERVER_USE_LOCAL_DAEMON` is a version-specific compatibility mechanism, not a permanent external API.
+
+## Current lifecycle maintenance
+
+`HAPI-desktop-maintenance` checks once a minute under the existing S4U user. A desktop, backend, package, CUA runtime or plugin generation change invalidates the old functional result and requests a fresh Session 0 execution probe. The probe launches a command under read-only, network-disabled permissions and confirms that a unique write attempt is denied. Healthy generations are reprobed every five minutes; failures back off to fifteen minutes. Checks write one bounded state file rather than an accumulating polling log.
+
+`DesktopContext.cs` returns only booleans for the current official desktop's authorization fields, live pipe and selected CLI. It never returns credentials. A missing desktop is `waiting-for-desktop`; maintenance does not reopen an application the user closed. An existing desktop gets two minutes to initialize. If its context stays unavailable, maintenance waits for active native turns to finish and requests the normal official desktop launcher to rebuild its context. Two failed attempts exhaust automatic recovery, with five minutes between attempts. A healthy context resets that count. A context check is not a browser functional result.
+
+`HAPI-desktop-runtime-update` handles installed package changes in a separate task so rollback can stop the maintenance task without terminating its own transaction. It checks native activity and fresh Session 0 DNS/HTTPS/WebSocket connectivity, stages the current installed package, and invokes `deploy-release.ps1`. Only exact-version, locally supplied sandbox repairs are eligible. Activation requires a new supervisor generation, native routing, real read-only sandbox execution, and the current desktop's authorization context when a desktop is open. Failed candidates restore the previous configuration and are not retried every minute. A candidate that fails execution or context checks is rejected; a candidate that passes still awaits separate functional acceptance. Future versions are never silently marked browser-compatible.
+
+The runtime selection, desktop scripts and stable environment are included in rollback. The current desktop package is never modified. In particular, do not replace `codex-command-runner.exe` inside `LOCALAPPDATA\OpenAI\Codex\bin`: the desktop validates that cache and can remove its companions while an old engine still locks `codex.exe`, preventing desktop initialization.
+
+The reviewed Session 0 helper repair and build catalog live in `patches/codex-sandbox-repairs.json` and `build-sandbox-repairs.py`. Builds use the exact official Rust tag and a locked dependency set; a repair for one engine version is not applied to another. The repair opens the current private window station instead of assuming `WinSta0`; it preserves restricted tokens, sandbox policies, pipe access controls and browser URL guards.
+
+Operational state is in `state\desktop-maintenance.json`, `state\desktop-runtime-update.json`, and `state\desktop-functional-current.json`. Only a real functional receipt matching the current generation changes `functionalAcceptance` to `verified`. See [the dated investigation and acceptance results](../../docs/operations/2026-10-28-windows-desktop-context.md) for live results and remaining regression boundaries.
diff --git a/scripts/windows/build-sandbox-repairs.py b/scripts/windows/build-sandbox-repairs.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..52e7883f9a7823df14c1ae1babb978998070456b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/scripts/windows/build-sandbox-repairs.py
@@ -0,0 +1,74 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""Build exact-version Session 0 helper bundles from reviewed upstream tags."""
+import argparse
+import json
+import os
+from pathlib import Path
+import shutil
+import subprocess
+import tarfile
+import tomllib
+import urllib.request
+
+
+def run(command, *, cwd, env, check=True):
+    return subprocess.run(command, cwd=cwd, env=env, check=check)
+
+
+def main():
+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()
+    parser.add_argument('--output', type=Path, required=True)
+    parser.add_argument('--cache', type=Path, default=Path('/mnt/cache/build-cache/hapi-codex-sandbox-repairs'))
+    options = parser.parse_args()
+    patches = Path(__file__).resolve().parent / 'patches'
+    catalog = json.loads((patches / 'codex-sandbox-repairs.json').read_text())
+    for repair in catalog['repairs']:
+        version = repair['engineVersion']
+        build = options.cache / version
+        build.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+        metadata = build / 'repair.json'
+        applied_patch = build / 'applied.patch'
+        binary = build / 'codex-command-runner.exe'
+        patch = patches / repair['patch']
+        cached = (binary.exists() and metadata.exists() and applied_patch.exists()
+                  and json.loads(metadata.read_text()) == repair
+                  and applied_patch.read_bytes() == patch.read_bytes())
+        if not cached:
+            archive = build / 'source.tar.gz'
+            if not archive.exists():
+                url = f"https://codeload.github.com/openai/codex/tar.gz/refs/tags/{repair['sourceTag']}"
+                urllib.request.urlretrieve(url, archive)
+            source = build / 'source'
+            source.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
+            with tarfile.open(archive) as bundle:
+                root = bundle.getmembers()[0].name.split('/')[0]
+                bundle.extractall(source, filter='data')
+            checkout = source / root
+            env = {**os.environ, 'RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN': os.environ.get('RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN', '1.96.0'),
+                   'CARGO_TARGET_DIR': str(options.cache / 'target'), 'TMPDIR': '/mnt/cache/data-cache'}
+            run(['patch', '--batch', '-p1', '-i', str(patch)], cwd=checkout, env=env)
+            lock = checkout / 'codex-rs/Cargo.lock'
+            external_before = [p for p in tomllib.loads(lock.read_text())['package'] if 'source' in p]
+            # Published tags can retain 0.0.0 for local workspace entries. Refresh
+            # those entries only; a missing offline dependency is fetched by the
+            # subsequent locked build. External dependency changes are rejected.
+            subprocess.run(['cargo', 'metadata', '--manifest-path', 'codex-rs/Cargo.toml', '--offline', '--format-version', '1'],
+                           cwd=checkout, env=env, check=False, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL)
+            external_after = [p for p in tomllib.loads(lock.read_text())['package'] if 'source' in p]
+            if external_before != external_after:
+                raise RuntimeError('External Cargo dependencies changed while refreshing local package versions')
+            run(['uvx', '--from', 'cargo-zigbuild', 'cargo-zigbuild', 'zigbuild', '--manifest-path',
+                 'codex-rs/Cargo.toml', '--package', 'codex-windows-sandbox', '--bin', 'codex-command-runner',
+                 '--target', 'x86_64-pc-windows-gnu', '--release', '--locked'], cwd=checkout, env=env)
+            shutil.copy2(options.cache / 'target/x86_64-pc-windows-gnu/release/codex-command-runner.exe', binary)
+            shutil.copy2(patch, applied_patch)
+            metadata.write_text(json.dumps(repair, indent=2) + '\n')
+        destination = options.output / version
+        destination.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+        shutil.copy2(binary, destination / binary.name)
+        shutil.copy2(metadata, destination / metadata.name)
+        print(f'Packaged Codex {version} Session 0 repair', flush=True)
+
+
+if __name__ == '__main__':
+    main()
diff --git a/scripts/windows/codex-runtime.ps1 b/scripts/windows/codex-runtime.ps1
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..9692268fbce31ffaa00ba054aa00abc27c9e2f59
--- /dev/null
+++ b/scripts/windows/codex-runtime.ps1
@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
+
+function Get-HapiManagedCodex {
+    param([string]$Root = 'D:\hapi')
+    $selection = Join-Path $Root 'config\codex-runtime.json'
+    if (!(Test-Path -LiteralPath $selection)) { return $null }
+    $runtime = Get-Content -LiteralPath $selection -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
+    $base = [IO.Path]::GetFullPath((Join-Path $Root 'runtimes\codex'))
+    $executable = [IO.Path]::GetFullPath([string]$runtime.executable)
+    if (!$executable.StartsWith($base + [IO.Path]::DirectorySeparatorChar, [StringComparison]::OrdinalIgnoreCase)) {
+        throw 'Selected Codex runtime is outside the HAPI runtime directory'
+    }
+    foreach ($name in $runtime.files) {
+        if ([IO.Path]::GetFileName([string]$name) -cne $name -or
+            !(Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path (Split-Path $executable) $name) -PathType Leaf)) {
+            throw 'Selected Codex runtime is incomplete'
+        }
+    }
+    return $runtime
+}
+
+function Install-HapiCodexRuntime {
+    param([Parameter(Mandatory)][string]$Root, [Parameter(Mandatory)][string]$Resources,
+        [Parameter(Mandatory)][string]$PackageVersion)
+    $source = Join-Path $Resources 'codex.exe'
+    $versionOutput = & $source --version
+    if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0 -or $versionOutput -notmatch '^codex-cli (\d+\.\d+\.\d+(?:-[0-9A-Za-z.]+)?)$') {
+        throw 'Cannot identify the installed official Codex runtime'
+    }
+    $engineVersion = $Matches[1]
+    $repair = Get-HapiSandboxRepair -Root $Root -EngineVersion $engineVersion
+    $revision = if ($repair) { $repair.revision } else { 'official' }
+    # Desktop owns and validates LOCALAPPDATA/OpenAI/Codex/bin. Never patch or
+    # run a long-lived HAPI engine there: desktop refresh can remove companions.
+    $directory = Join-Path $Root ('runtimes\codex\' + $engineVersion + '-' + $revision + '-' + $PackageVersion)
+    $required = @('codex.exe', 'codex-code-mode-host.exe', 'codex-command-runner.exe', 'codex-windows-sandbox-setup.exe')
+    $files = @(Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath $Resources -File | Where-Object {$_.Extension -in @('.exe', '.dll')} | Select-Object -ExpandProperty Name)
+    foreach ($name in $required) { if ($files -notcontains $name) { throw "Official runtime is missing $name" } }
+    $manifestPath = Join-Path $directory 'runtime.json'
+    if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $manifestPath) {
+        $existing = Get-Content -LiteralPath $manifestPath -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
+        if ($existing.engineVersion -eq $engineVersion -and $existing.revision -eq $revision -and
+            @($existing.files | Where-Object {!(Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path (Join-Path $directory 'bin') $_) -PathType Leaf)}).Count -eq 0) {
+            return $existing
+        }
+        throw 'Existing HAPI runtime is incomplete; leave the active engine untouched'
+    }
+    $staging = "$directory.staging-$([Guid]::NewGuid().ToString('N'))"
+    New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path (Join-Path $staging 'bin') -Force | Out-Null
+    try {
+        foreach ($name in $files) { Copy-Item -LiteralPath (Join-Path $Resources $name) -Destination (Join-Path $staging 'bin') }
+        if ($repair) { Copy-Item -LiteralPath $repair.executable -Destination (Join-Path $staging 'bin\codex-command-runner.exe') -Force }
+        $runtime = [pscustomobject]@{version=1; engineVersion=$engineVersion; packageVersion=$PackageVersion;
+            revision=$revision; files=$files; executable=(Join-Path $directory 'bin\codex.exe')}
+        $runtime | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 5 | Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $staging 'runtime.json') -Encoding utf8NoBOM
+        Move-Item -LiteralPath $staging -Destination $directory
+        return $runtime
+    } finally {
+        if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $staging) { Remove-Item -LiteralPath $staging -Recurse -Force }
+    }
+}
+
+function Select-HapiCodexRuntime {
+    param([Parameter(Mandatory)][string]$Root, [Parameter(Mandatory)]$Runtime)
+    $selection = Join-Path $Root 'config\codex-runtime.json'
+    $Runtime | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 5 | Set-Content -LiteralPath "$selection.next" -Encoding utf8NoBOM
+    Move-Item -LiteralPath "$selection.next" -Destination $selection -Force
+}
